  faqs: [
    { question: "Where does a Kharagpur family actually find an IB tutor?", answer: "Send over the programme, subject, level and exam session your child is working toward, and a shortlist comes back built entirely from tutors who have taught that precise course before. Location plays no part in it, since nowhere in Kharagpur teaches the IB anyway; what matters is finding an evening slot that suits your household and letting a free trial lesson confirm the fit before anything is agreed." },
    { question: "Can Kharagpur students get IGCSE tuition for both Cambridge and Edexcel?", answer: "Yes, and the two are treated as genuinely separate systems, not variations on a theme. A Cambridge student is matched by code and tier, say Mathematics 0580 Extended or Chemistry 0620, while an Edexcel student is matched by specification and Foundation or Higher tier, with each board's own past papers and mark schemes driving the actual lessons." },
    { question: "Will a tutor come to our house in Kharagpur?", answer: "No. That arrangement is reserved for Gurugram and a handful of neighbourhoods in Delhi NCR. Everywhere else, Kharagpur included, lessons run live on video, one to one, with a shared digital whiteboard doing what a notebook on the table would otherwise do. It is real, personal tuition, just conducted through a screen rather than at your door." },
    { question: "How much should IB or IGCSE tutoring cost for a Kharagpur student?", answer: "The number moves with the programme, the subject, how long a session runs and how uncommon it is to find someone who has recently taught that exact course, with Diploma HL subjects usually sitting above MYP or IGCSE Core for that reason. Whatever it works out to is confirmed before the trial lesson, has no travel charge hidden in it since everything runs online, and never locks you into a fixed-term contract." },
    { question: "Is there truly no school in Kharagpur teaching IB or Cambridge IGCSE?", answer: "Correct, at least as far as schoolmykids.com's listings go, which show nothing in the city against either curriculum. What Kharagpur has instead is West Bengal Board and CBSE schooling, largely built around IIT Kharagpur and the railway colony, DAV Model School and a Kendriya Vidyalaya among the recognisable names. Anyone here pursuing IB or IGCSE is almost certainly doing so through a distance provider, which is exactly why our own tutoring never assumes a physical campus in the background." },
    { question: "If Kharagpur has no IB school, where do families actually look instead?", answer: "Plenty simply stay put and pair an online IB or IGCSE provider with tutoring to fill whatever gets left thin. Others start looking toward secondary school with Kolkata in mind, about 120 kilometres away and home to the state's real cluster of established IB and Cambridge schools, with Bhubaneswar sitting further out as a second possibility." },
    { question: "Do you actually let us try before paying anything?", answer: "Every single match begins that way. Your child sits through one genuine lesson on real syllabus content with no money changing hands and no obligation attached, after which the tutor writes up a short plan for the first month. From there it is entirely your call, proceed, request tweaks, or ask for someone different." },
    { question: "Will a tutor write parts of my child's Internal Assessment for them?", answer: "No, and this is not negotiable. What a tutor will do is help settle on a workable research question, explain exactly what an assessment criterion is looking for, help plan how data gets gathered, and give straight feedback on drafts. Producing or rewriting the assessed work itself would breach IB academic integrity rules, so it simply is not offered." },
    { question: "Which Diploma subjects come up most for students connected to Kharagpur?", answer: "Every major subject group is covered, though Maths, in either Analysis and Approaches or Applications and Interpretation, alongside Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management, English A and Computer Science, account for most enquiries, with Theory of Knowledge and Extended Essay support layered in alongside." },
    { question: "Is support available for MYP and PYP students in Kharagpur too, not just the Diploma?", answer: "Yes, right across the continuum. At MYP level, help usually centres on criterion-based writing in the sciences and Language and Literature, plus the Personal Project journal; at PYP level, it is reading, writing, number confidence and Exhibition research skills, generally in shorter, more frequent sessions suited to a younger student." },
    { question: "Does a video lesson actually work as well as sitting with a tutor face to face?", answer: "For IB and IGCSE specifically, yes, not just as an online substitute, given how few genuine specialists exist in a city this size for HL subjects or particular IGCSE codes. Home visits are never part of the offer outside Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR anyway, so a shared whiteboard, live screen-shared past papers and recorded solutions carry the weight instead, while the pool of available specialists grows from a handful locally to hundreds nationally." },
    { question: "What actually stops IB Gram from sending an unqualified tutor?", answer: "A screening step before any family meets anyone: qualifications confirmed, recent experience with that specific subject and level checked, and their approach to Internal Assessment guidance reviewed. Because Kharagpur's local pool is close to nonexistent, the bar for 'recently taught this exact syllabus' is applied strictly rather than loosely, and the trial lesson gives you a final, direct check yourself." },
    { question: "What is the right age or year to begin IB or IGCSE tutoring from Kharagpur?", answer: "Ideally right when the course itself starts, Class 11 for the Diploma and Grade 9 for IGCSE, since that leaves room to fix gaps before internal exams, IA deadlines and predicted grades all land. Joining later, even in the final year, still helps meaningfully if the sessions focus tightly on the highest-yield topics and past papers rather than trying to cover everything." },
    { question: "My child is switching from the West Bengal Board or CBSE into IB or IGCSE. What actually changes?", answer: "Mostly the way a question is asked, not the underlying content. Command words like 'explain', 'evaluate' and 'justify' carry specific meanings under IB and IGCSE marking that board-exam preparation rarely covers, and coursework planning is an entirely new skill on top of that. Starting the summer before the move gives a tutor room to build both before term begins." },
    { question: "What times actually work for sessions given Kharagpur's schedule?", answer: "Weekday evenings after school and weekend mornings cover most families here. Connectivity can dip during the heaviest monsoon weeks, and Durga Puja effectively pauses everything for a stretch, so both get built into the plan rather than ignored. Slotting in a second weekly session ahead of mocks is a quick adjustment, not a renegotiation." },
    { question: "What happens if the assigned tutor just isn't clicking with my child?", answer: "You tell us, and a different tutor gets found. Check-ins happen every few weeks specifically to catch this early, and switching is treated as routine rather than a failure worth dwelling on. Since nothing is locked into a long contract, pausing entirely while a better match is found costs nothing either." },
    { question: "Does IB Gram have any tie to IIT Kharagpur, a local school, or the IB and Cambridge bodies?", answer: "None whatsoever. IB Gram operates as an independent tutoring service with no affiliation to IIT Kharagpur, to any school referenced on this page, or to the International Baccalaureate Organization, Cambridge Assessment International Education or Pearson Edexcel. References to any of them here are purely descriptive, explaining the landscape a Kharagpur family is actually navigating, and tutors work strictly to each provider's own published calendar and syllabus." },
  ],

